    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It represents a one-directional relationship between two vertices."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It has a starting vertex and an ending vertex. So, they are represented using arrowheads pointing from the starting vertex to the end vertex."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Arrow Represents Directed Edge",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In the above graph, we can traverse from A to B but not from B to A."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For example, a one-way route that only allows you to travel in a single direction."
